**Posterior predictive check.** `remove_unwanted_effects = TRUE` removes variation other than biopsy timepoint, so the black boxes are adjusted proportions and the blue boxes are posterior predictive replicates. Fill marks a timepoint contrast with FDR below 0.05.


::: {.cell layout-align="center"}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false" code-summary="Posterior predictive check"}
fit |> 
  sccomp_boxplot(
  factor = "BiopsyPhase",
  significance_statistic = "FDR",
  remove_unwanted_effects = TRUE
  ) +
  labs(
    title = "Posterior predictive check",
    subtitle = "Black: adjusted proportions. Blue: replicates from the fitted model.",
    x = "Biopsy timepoint"
  ) +
  guides(colour = "none", shape = "none") 
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](index_files/figure-html/repro-ppc-1.png){fig-align='center' fig-alt='Boxplots of immune-cell proportions by biopsy timepoint, faceted by cell type, after removing variation other than biopsy timepoint. Black boxes are adjusted proportions and blue boxes are posterior predictive replicates. Filled boxes mark a timepoint contrast with FDR below 0.05.'}
