Post-treatment M2 levels alone look similar between the two groups (21.9% in pCR vs 18.2% in RD among the displayed patients; 22.8% vs 20.9% across the cohort). The signal is in the change from baseline (**Figure 2**) rather than the single-visit cross-section.

